  |         ^^^^^^^^ expected one of cartesian, flip, polar, fixed

== coordinates_in_quotation_marks
error[Z0403]: expected one of cartesian, flip, polar, fixed, found text
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:9
  |
3 | p.coord("flip")
  |         ^^^^^^ a word, not a string
  |
  = help: write the word without quotes: `flip`

== coordinates_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `coord` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | d.coord(flip)
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `coord` takes a Plot first; `x.coord(...)` is `coord(x, ...)`

== polar_not_built_yet
error[Z0401]: `coord(polar)` is not built yet: it comes with a later step of this release
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:9
  |
3 | p.coord(polar)
  |         ^^^^^ not in this build
  |
  = help: the coordinates built so far are `cartesian`, `flip` and `fixed`

== a_ratio_without_fixed
error[Z0401]: `ratio:` of `coord` goes with `fixed`, but the coordinates are `cartesian`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:16
  |
3 | p.coord(ratio: 2)
  |                ^ a ratio without `fixed`
  |
  = help: write `coord(fixed, ratio: 2)` for a panel in which a unit of `y` is as long as two units of `x`; the other coordinates take the shape of the page

== a_ratio_with_flip
error[Z0401]: `ratio:` of `coord` goes with `fixed`, but the coordinates are `flip`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:22
  |
3 | p.coord(flip, ratio: 2)
  |                      ^ a ratio without `fixed`
  |
  = help: write `coord(fixed, ratio: 2)` for a panel in which a unit of `y` is as long as two units of `x`; the other coordinates take the shape of the page

== a_ratio_of_zero
error[Z0401]: `ratio:` of `coord` is how many units of `x` are as long as one unit of `y`, and must be above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:23
  |
3 | p.coord(fixed, ratio: 0)
  |                       ^ not a ratio
  |
  = help: `coord(fixed)` gives a unit of `y` the length of a unit of `x`; `coord(fixed, ratio: 2)` makes a unit of `y` twice as long, and `ratio: 0.5` half as long

== a_ratio_below_zero
error[Z0401]: `ratio:` of `coord` is how many units of `x` are as long as one unit of `y`, and must be above 0, but this is -1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:23
  |
3 | p.coord(fixed, ratio: -1)
  |                       ^^ not a ratio
  |
  = help: `coord(fixed)` gives a unit of `y` the length of a unit of `x`; `coord(fixed, ratio: 2)` makes a unit of `y` twice as long, and `ratio: 0.5` half as long

== a_ratio_that_is_text
error[Z0401]: `ratio` of `coord` must be a Float, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:23
  |
3 | p.coord(fixed, ratio: "square")
  |                       ^^^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `p.coord(type: cartesian | flip | polar | fixed = cartesian, ratio: Float)`

== a_panel_too_thin
error[Z0401]: fixed coordinates make the panel of this plot 420 times as high as it is wide: on a page of 89 by 66 mm that is 0.1 by 52 mm
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | export(d.plot(x: dose, y: change).points().coord(fixed, ratio: 500), "thin.svg")
  | ^^^^^^ too thin a panel
  |
  = help: a panel needs 12.7 mm each way; `coord(fixed, ratio: 0.85)` fills this page, and a plot whose two axes do not share a unit needs no `coord(fixed)`

== a_panel_too_flat
error[Z0401]: fixed coordinates make the panel of this plot 600 times as wide as it is high: on a page of 89 by 66 mm that is 73.3 by 0.1 mm
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | export(d.plot(x: dose, y: change).points().coord(fixed, ratio: 0.002), "flat.svg")
  | ^^^^^^ too thin a panel
  |
  = help: a panel needs 12.7 mm each way; `coord(fixed, ratio: 0.85)` fills this page, and a plot whose two axes do not share a unit needs no `coord(fixed)`

